{"packet_id": "D069-01", "doc_id": "D069", "jurisdiction": "NJ", "category": "algorithmic_rent_setting", "lifecycle": "enacted", "title": "FAIR Act ban on coordinator services and algorithmic rent setting", "requirement": "No rental property owner, agent, representative or subcontractor may exchange consideration for the services of a coordinator performing a coordinating function over residential dwelling units. The act takes effect the first day of the twelfth month after enactment.", "key_value": null, "coverage_conditions": "All residential dwelling units in New Jersey, meaning any house, apartment, accessory unit or other unit intended for use as a primary residence, excluding medical, long-term care and detention facilities.", "applicability": {"built_on_or_before": null, "built_after": null, "date_basis": null, "min_units": null, "max_units": null, "owner_dependent": false, "other": null}, "exemptions": "Coordinating function excludes research or statistical analysis, published rent estimates made available to the public at no cost, listing databases offered on equal terms and government affordability controls; spreadsheets and query-only databases are not algorithmic devices.", "penalty": "A violation is a violation of the New Jersey Antitrust Act and does not limit the application of sections 6 through 17 of P.L.1970, c.73; the Attorney General must maintain a website location to receive complaints.", "effective_date": null, "citation": "P.L. 2026, c.43 § 4", "quoted_span": "shall be unlawful and a violation of the “New Jersey Antitrust Act,” P.L.1970,
c.73 (C.56:9-1 et seq.) for:
a.     a rental property owner, or any agent,
representative, or subcontractor thereof, to receive, subscribe to, contract
for, or otherwise exchange any form of consideration in return for the use of,
the services of a coordinator;", "interaction": "Construed in addition to the New Jersey Antitrust Act, which continues to apply to the same conduct.", "confidence": 0.95, "conflict_flag": false, "conflict_note": null}
